  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-claude-subscription",
      "text": "Use Claude models in [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) through your Claude subscription account."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-claude-subscription",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source\n      media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n      srcset=\"images/claude-account-usage-dark.png\"\n    >\n    <img\n      alt=\"The /claude-account card showing a signed-in Claude account and its token expiry, and the /claude-usage card showing the 5-hour and weekly quota windows\"\n      src=\"images/claude-account-usage-light.png\"\n      width=\"754\"\n    >\n  </picture>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-claude-subscription",
      "text": "> [!WARNING]\n> This project is not official. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Anthropic or DeepSeek Harness, and it comes with no warranty, support, or liability."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/apcamargo/dsh-claude-subscription.git\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Getting started",
      "text": "Sign in from any session:\n\n```\n/claude-login\n```\n\nIt prints an authorization link and opens it in your browser. Approve it there to grant the plugin access to your subscription."
    },
    {
      "section": "Using multiple accounts",
      "text": "You can run `/claude-login` multiple times to add additional accounts. Each one becomes its own group in the model picker, labeled with the email associated with it.\n\nWhichever account is signed in at [claude.ai](https://claude.ai/) in your browser is the one that gets added. Sign in to the account you want first, or open the authorization link in a private window."
    },
    {
      "section": "Commands",
      "text": "| Command                           | What it does                                     |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `/claude-login [email]`           | Sign in, add an account, or refresh a credential |\n| `/claude-account [account]`       | Show the signed-in account and token expiry      |\n| `/claude-usage [account]`         | Show quota usage and reset times                 |\n| `/claude-logout [account\\|--all]` | Sign out and delete the stored credentials       |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage indicator",
      "text": "When the selected model belongs to a subscription account, a small Claude mark appears in the message composer to the left of its model selector. Its colored fill drains as your primary quota has been used, and clicking it opens a panel with detailed information."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage indicator",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source\n      media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n      srcset=\"images/claude-usage-indicator-dark.png\"\n    >\n    <img\n      alt=\"The Claude mark in the composer with its quota panel open, showing the 5-hour and weekly windows\"\n      src=\"images/claude-usage-indicator-light.png\"\n      width=\"424\"\n    >\n  </picture>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Models page",
      "text": "The plugin adds a \"Claude subscription\" section to the Models page in Settings. It lists each signed-in account, the model catalog, and lets you edit the model list per account."
    },
    {
      "section": "Models page",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source\n      media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n      srcset=\"images/claude-models-card-dark.png\"\n    >\n    <img\n      alt=\"The Claude subscription section of the Models page: a signed-in account with its plan and the model list state\"\n      src=\"images/claude-models-card-light.png\"\n      width=\"823\"\n    >\n  </picture>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install"
    },
    {
      "section": "Rebuild lib/client.js and executes unit tests",
      "text": "npm test"
    },
    {
      "section": "Mount the plugin through the real cordis runtime",
      "text": "npm run verify"
    },
    {
      "section": "Regenerate lib/client.js after editing client-app.js or client-models.js",
      "text": "npm run build:client"
    },
    {
      "section": "Regenerate the README figures using a local headless Chromium",
      "text": "npm run images\n```"
    }
  ],
